1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,360
One penny beats a million dollars. But first, it tortures you.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,600
Here's the deal. You can take a million dollars today.

3
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:12,680
Or you take one penny that doubles every day for thirty days, no taxes.

4
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:18,440
Doubling means you get the same amount again. So one penny turns into two, then four.

5
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:22,880
So day three, you've got four cents. Day four, it's eight cents.

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:24,840
Hit like if you'd grab the penny.

7
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:29,100
Sounds tiny, right? After a week, you've got sixty-four cents.

8
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:33,200
Day ten, you're at five dollars and twelve cents. That's one coffee.

9
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:35,200
By day twenty, you've got about five thousand dollars.

10
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:40,600
And that million you skipped is still about a hundred ninety times bigger.

11
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,220
Send this to the friend who'd quit right here.

12
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:46,580
Now it gets painful. Day twenty-seven, you're at six hundred seventy-one thousand dollars.

13
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:53,000
Three days left, and you're still— you're still losing to the million.

14
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,880
Follow, this page always finishes the math.

15
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:59,260
Day twenty-eight, the penny finally passes the million.

16
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:02,540
And day thirty? Five point three seven million dollars.

17
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:07,020
Almost all of it, seven eighths, showed up in those last three days.

18
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:10,540
So be honest. On day twenty, are you still holding that penny?

